==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɔɪnt}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# not smooth or [[continuous]]; [[disjointed]]
# {{settheory}} (''not used in the comparative or superlative'') Of two or more [[set]]s, having no members in common; having an [[intersection]] equal to the [[empty set]].

====Antonyms====
* [[non-disjoint]]
* [[overlapping]]

====Translations====
{{trans-top|having no members in common}}
* Chinese: [[不相交的]]
* Czech: {{t-|cs|disjunktní|m}}
{{trans-mid}}
* German: {{t+|de|disjunkt}}
* Korean: [[서로소]] (seoroso)
{{trans-bottom}}

====Related terms====
* [[disjunct]]
* [[conjoint]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# to render [[disjoint#Adjective|disjoint]]; to remove a connection, linkage, or intersection

====Translations====
* Bulgarian: [[разглобявам]]
* German: [[zertrennen]]
* Korean: [[해체하다]] (haechehada)

